    @Test
    void pathExclusionKeepsNameRequiredByOtherPathAndWithdrawOfItBreaksLock() {
        // 合成根同时依赖 a 和 b：root->a 排除 c，root->b 仍需要 c。
        service.registerArtifact(requestId(),
                artifact("root", 1, depx("a", 1, 1, "c"), dep("b", 1, 1)));
        service.registerArtifact(requestId(), artifact("a", 1, dep("c", 1, 1)));
        service.registerArtifact(requestId(), artifact("b", 1, dep("c", 1, 1)));
        service.registerArtifact(requestId(), artifact("c", 1));

        LockFileResponse lock = service.createLock(requestId(), new LockRequest("root", 1, 4L));
        assertThat(lock.entries()).extracting("name", "version")
                .containsExactly(tuple("a", 1), tuple("b", 1), tuple("c", 1), tuple("root", 1));
        // 保留边含 b->c 不含 a->c。
        assertThat(lock.edges()).extracting("fromName", "toName")
                .contains(tuple("root", "a"), tuple("root", "b"), tuple("b", "c"))
                .doesNotContain(tuple("a", "c"));
        // 排除理由落库：root->a 排除 c 实际忽略了 a->c。
        assertThat(lock.exclusions()).singleElement().satisfies(record -> {
            assertThat(record.fromName()).isEqualTo("root");
            assertThat(record.toName()).isEqualTo("a");
            assertThat(record.excludedName()).isEqualTo("c");
            assertThat(record.outcome()).isEqualTo("APPLIED");
            assertThat(record.detail()).contains("a->c");
        });
        // 历史查询与创建响应一致（后续变更不改旧解释）。
        assertThat(service.getLock(lock.id())).isEqualTo(lock);

        // 撤回唯一的 c 后，锁定必须失败（b 路径仍需要 c）。
        service.withdrawArtifact(requestId(), "c", 1);
        assertThatThrownBy(() -> service.createLock(requestId(), new LockRequest("root", 1, 5L)))
                .isInstanceOfSatisfying(ApiException.class,
                        e -> assertThat(e.getStatus()).isEqualTo(422));
        assertThat(jdbcTemplate.queryForObject("SELECT COUNT(1) FROM lock_file", Integer.class))
                .isEqualTo(1);
    }
```

Wait — getLock(lock.id()) equals lock? LockFileResponse record equality: entries/edges/exclusions lists — created response built from solution; queried built from DB rows. Order: entries both name-sorted ✓; edges: solution edges sorted by fromName,fromVersion,toName; DB query same ORDER BY ✓; exclusions same ✓. createdAt: Instant — stored as TIMESTAMP(6) and read back. H2 TIMESTAMP(6) stores micros; Instant.now(clock) has nanos. Equality may fail due to truncation! createdAt in response = now (nanos); DB read = truncated to micros. On most systems Instant.now() has micro or nano precision... Windows clock precision ~ms or better. Risky. Existing test `lockProducesSortedEntriesAndPersistsRepositoryVersion` compares `service.getLock(lock.id()).entries()` — only entries, not full object. And `lockReplayAfterUnrelatedChanges...` compares replay.id() and entries. So avoid full-object equality; compare entries/edges/exclusions separately. I'll assert getLock(lock.id()).edges() equals lock.edges() and exclusions equal, entries equal.

